~/vm-bake/guest
# @summary The guests' views of the invoking user's home: VM_BAKE_VIEW_DIR/<guest> is one ZFS dataset per guest, which the guest mounts over virtio-9p as the whole home of its host-uid user when its template says 'service files view'. A leading ~/ is the invoking user's home. 'guest view tree ensure' makes the datasets that carry the views, once per host: beside the dataset that carries the home, under its parent, with this path below the home as the dataset path, slash for slash -- <parent>/vm-bake/guest for ~/vm-bake/guest; the head of that path carries the mount point, everything below inherits it, and 'guest view ensure' then creates <parent>/vm-bake/guest/<guest>. A view is a dataset of its own and therefore NOT in the snapshots of the home's dataset: a backup has to take the parent recursively. What the guest writes there (its dotfiles, the state of its tools) lies in the home -- its clones do not, they lie on its disk under VM_BAKE_REPO_LOCAL, because git cannot write its objects on p9fs; what it may see of the rest of the home is the template's home list, hung into the view by 'guest start' as nullfs overlays and let go by 'guest stop'.
